==Battleground==
*1 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cat]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[Ginger Snache]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 20.67 seconds<sup>620f</sup>, delay 3.33~10.67 seconds<sup>100f~320f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cat]] spawns.
**40 [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cats]] spawn, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cats]] spawn, delay 4~8 seconds<sup>120f~240f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is just a beefed-up version of [[Head Shaker (Insane)]], and as such the general strategy remains the same: stall the first Manic Lion Cat until your wallet is full, hit the enemy base, lure the Lions close, then start spamming everything you have, be it meatshields or [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]]. If the stack grows sufficiently you can accumulate enough DPS to quickly cripple the Manic Lions and win the stage.

The Manic Lion Cats are still single-target and outranged by almost every cat, so you're putting yourself at a disadvantage if you're not using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]]. Of course, they still have to be protected well and serve as support instead of your main damage source.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Spammable Area Attackers such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and the [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]] should form the core of your offense. Large stacks of them will deal enough damage to turn the battle in your favor.
*If one were to own the elusive [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed UFO Cat]], its insanely high DPS against Traitless enemies will tear through the Manic Lions with ease, and the mini-wave helps a lot for extra chip.
*[[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]], [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], [[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Macho Suntan Cat]], [[Lifeguard Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Sweet Bro Cats]], [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Glass Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] are able to provide adequate defense with their abilities, though in some cases it may be better to add another attacker instead as they all have a major disadvantage that must be accounted for.
**If you decide to use Healer or Headmaster Cat Jobs, be wary; they both have extremely low survivability and need their own respective [[Cat Combo|Combos]]; [[Pumpkinpants (Combo)|Pumpkinpants]] & [[Gross!!! (Combo)|Gross!!!]] for Healer and [[Power of Darkness (Combo)|Power of Darkness]] for Headmaster. Adding to this is a second layer of luck for Headmaster; you may have to try again for his [[Surge Attack|Surges]] to spawn on the Manic Lions in the right place.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Nezuko Kamado (Uber Rare Cat)|Nezuko Kamado]]: She outranges the Manic Lion Cats and can control them reliably with her knockback. Nezuko is basically a perfect counter to this stage.
*Unsurprisingly, many [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusive units can make this stage much easier due to being catered specifically against traitless enemies. However, they have their own issues and are not meant to be used alone. [[Dark Aegis Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Garu]] is only able to tank for a little while without much direct damage, [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli]], [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] and [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]] have blindspots that must be factored in, [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]]'s freeze has little uptime and won't stop the lions from pushing and he and [[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Eventide]] have rather long attack rates, while [[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz]] doesn't have much range to begin with.

